## 📦 Deployment Steps

### Step 1: Prepare AWS Account

```bash
# 1. Create S3 bucket for deployment
aws s3 mb s3://mshauri-deployment-us-east-1 --region us-east-1

# 2. Create S3 bucket for feedback (training data)
aws s3 mb s3://mshauri-feedback-prod --region us-east-1

# 3. Enable Bedrock access
aws bedrock create-provisioned-model-throughput \
  --provisioned-model-name mshauri-throughput \
  --model-units 1 \
  --model-id anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022

# 4. Store secrets in AWS Secrets Manager
aws secretsmanager create-secret \
  --name TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID \
  --secret-string "your_twilio_sid"

aws secretsmanager create-secret \
  --name AFRICASTALKING_API_KEY \
  --secret-string "your_at_api_key"
```

### Step 2: Deploy Infrastructure

```bash
# 1. Export deployment files
python deployment_config.py export

# 2. Build Lambda package
sam build --use-container --parameter-overrides Environment=dev

# 3. Deploy CloudFormation stack
sam deploy \
  --stack-name ai-mshauri-dev \
  --region us-east-1 \
  --capabilities CAPABILITY_IAM CAPABILITY_NAMED_IAM \
  --parameter-overrides Environment=dev

# 4. Verify deployment
aws cloudformation describe-stacks \
  --stack-name ai-mshauri-dev \
  --query 'Stacks[0].StackStatus'
```

### Step 3: Configure API Gateway

```bash
# 1. Get API ID
API_ID=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks \
  --stack-name ai-mshauri-dev \
  --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey==`MshuariApiId`].OutputValue' \
  --output text)

# 2. Get API Key
API_KEY=$(aws cloudformation describe-stacks \
  --stack-name ai-mshauri-dev \
  --query 'Stacks[0].Outputs[?OutputKey==`MshuariApiKey`].OutputValue' \
  --output text)

# 3. Test endpoint
curl -X POST \
  https://$API_ID.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/dev/mentorship \
  -H "x-api-key: $API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "phone_number": "+254712345678",
    "sauti_output": "You have wage rights under Employment Act 2007",
    "category": "wage_rights",
    "county": "Kisumu",
    "language": "sw"
  }'
```

### Step 4: Setup SageMaker Training

```bash
# 1. Create SageMaker notebook instance
aws sagemaker create-notebook-instance \
  --notebook-instance-name mshauri-training \
  --instance-type ml.t3.medium \
  --role-arn arn:aws:iam::YOUR_ACCOUNT:role/SageMakerRole

# 2. Upload training script
aws s3 cp sagemaker_training.py s3://mshauri-feedback-prod/scripts/

# 3. Run training pipeline
python -c "
from sagemaker_training import TrainingPipeline
import sagemaker

pipeline = TrainingPipeline(
    s3_bucket='mshauri-feedback-prod',
    role_arn=sagemaker.get_execution_role(),
    region='us-east-1'
)
results = pipeline.run()
"
```

